From: FORZA-LAUNCHER-FOR-MAC-BLACKWELL-PROJECT
Subject: [PATCH] run: On macOS keep the decrypted image's name on the RAM disk.

Applies to xodus-gaming/xodus 3e75c9f (the commit Ferestre pins) after
Ferestre's patches/xodus-cli 0002-0027 (0001 is skipped, as Ferestre's
scripts/check-patches.sh does).

On macOS the decrypted image went into tempfile_in(<RAM disk>), which deletes
the name immediately. Wine needs a name to give each handle on the image its
own file position (no /proc on macOS; see
patches/wine/0001-ntdll-macos-reopen-mapped-image-by-path.patch). The file
now keeps its name inside the private, nobrowse RAM disk, which is
force-detached when the game exits, so the plaintext still never reaches a
persistent disk. Linux (memfd) and other systems are unchanged.

Not compiled for macOS here unless docs/ANALYSE-FH6-STORE-MACOS.md says so.
